#: ../../../CIR/index.md:1
msgid "ClangIR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/index.md:3
msgid ""
"ClangIR (CIR) is a high-level representation in Clang that reflects aspects "
"of the C/C++ languages and their extensions. It is implemented using MLIR "
"and occupies a position between Clang's AST and LLVM IR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/index.md:7
msgid ""
"Follow and contribute to upstream development through the [`ClangIR`-labeled "
"issues and pull requests](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/labels/"
"ClangIR) on llvm-project. See the [ClangIR Design Documents](#clangir-design-"
"documents) for in-depth coverage of CIR's design."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/index.md:13
msgid "Using ClangIR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/index.md:15
msgid ""
"ClangIR is an MLIR dialect tightly integrated with Clang: it lives in the "
"Clang project rather than as a standalone in-tree dialect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/index.md:18
msgid ""
"Pass `-fclangir` to the Clang driver to compile through CIR (AST to CIR to "
"CIR passes to LLVM IR and the backend). In order to inspect CIR output, use "
"`-emit-cir`, the equivalent of `-emit-llvm` for CIR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/index.md:23
msgid ""
"ClangIR can be disabled from the build of Clang via the `-"
"DCLANG_ENABLE_CIR=OFF`, see [CMake](https://llvm.org/docs/CMake.html) flag. "
"Using this flag can reduce the compile time and binary size of Clang, "
"however it will make the `-fclangir` flag unavaiable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/index.md:28
msgid ""
"See this [Compiler Explorer example](https://godbolt.org/z/dTGqMGx54), which "
"shows the flow of compilation through CIR, from higher-level CIR constructs "
"to lower-level ones, the pipeline viewer is convenient for following along."
msgstr ""

